<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reginald Johnston</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1874">1874</a>–<a href="/years/1938">1938</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reginald Johnston was a Scottish colonial official and scholar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. From 1919 to 1924 he was tutor to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puyi">Puyi</a>, the last Qing emperor, in the Forbidden City, and described this in Twilight in the Forbidden City. He then served as commissioner of the British leased territory of Weihaiwei until its return to China in 1930, and later taught Chinese in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reginald-johnston.jpg" alt="Reginald Johnston" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Scan: Kenmayer, Original: unnamed photographer, likely under hire by the Imperial Household of the deposed Emperor w:Puyi. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reginald_Johnston.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
